Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Note: Syl System Standard Library v1.4
Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Note: Provides file system, process, and OS interaction primitives.
Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Note: ─── Platform Detection ───────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "platform" that does:
    Return "windows".

Define an action called "arch" that does:
    Return "x86_64".

Note: ─── File System ──────────────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "read_file" taking path that does:
    Read path as content.
    Return content.

Define an action called "write_file" taking path and data that does:
    Write data to path.

Define an action called "list_files" taking dir that does:
    List files in dir as entries.
    Return entries.

Define an action called "file_exists" taking path that does:
    Set s to the size of path.
    Return s.

Note: ─── Directory Operations ─────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "mkdir" taking path that does:
    Create folder path.

Define an action called "move_file" taking src and dst that does:
    Move src to dst.

Note: ─── Process ──────────────────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "exit" taking code that does:
    Print "Exiting with code " joined with code.
